WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.525
Radar is the only instrument aboard that shows you what’s actually out there right now.

2
00:00:05.775 --> 00:00:09.000
Not what was charted, and not what’s broadcasting.

3
00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:10.775
What’s there.

4
00:00:11.025 --> 00:00:12.775
Here’s how it works.

5
00:00:13.025 --> 00:00:17.575
It sends out pulses of microwave energy, and times the echoes.

6
00:00:17.825 --> 00:00:19.550
Look at the display.

7
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.900
Your boat is at the center.

8
00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:26.875
The line pointing up is your heading line, and the circles are range rings.

9
00:00:27.125 --> 00:00:29.925
Radar measures range very accurately.

10
00:00:30.175 --> 00:00:34.975
It measures bearing a little less accurately, because the beam has some width.

11
00:00:35.225 --> 00:00:37.300
Two tools do the measuring.

12
00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:43.875
The variable range marker, the V R M, is a circle you set on a target to read its range.

13
00:00:44.125 --> 00:00:50.350
The electronic bearing line, the E B L, is a line you lay through a target to read its bearing.

14
00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:53.325
Now tie it to the Rules.

15
00:00:53.575 --> 00:00:56.000
You put the E B L on a target.

16
00:00:56.250 --> 00:01:00.200
The target slides down that line toward you, never leaving it.

17
00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:02.200
What does that mean?

18
00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:04.900
Steady bearing, closing range.

19
00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:07.000
Risk of collision.
